<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mayta Capac</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 13th–14th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mayta Capac was the fourth ruler of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> tradition, the son of Lloque Yupanqui. The chronicles describe him as a strong warrior who fought the neighbouring Alcabizas and other peoples of the Cusco valley. Like the other early Inca rulers, he is known only from traditions recorded by Spanish chroniclers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mayta-capac.jpg" alt="Mayta Capac" width="221" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio de Herrera y Tordesillas (1549 - c.1625/26) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mayta_Capac.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
